  "request": {
    "spec": "When a clerk settles a claim whose due is above the clerk limit, the claim now goes to PENDING\ninstead of being refused (CLAIM_PENDING, naming the claim like every claim line). A PENDING claim\ncounts as open in every total, but is not bound by a statement: while PENDING it shows and totals\nits live figure. A steward approves it (it becomes SETTLED, frozen at that moment, CLAIM_APPROVED\nwith due=<due> at the end like CLAIM_SETTLED) or rejects it with a reason (back to OPEN, bound\nagain by the last statement if that statement included it, CLAIM_REJECTED with reason=<reason> at\nthe end). The opener cannot approve their own claim. In every other way a PENDING claim is handled\nlike an OPEN one: it cannot be edited, it can be voided (CLAIM_VOIDED), it goes overdue and bears\nthe late charge, and a hold takes it out of the totals.\n",
    "prompt": "You are implementing ONE change to this application.\n\nFIRST read AGENTS.md \u2014 it states the working rules and how the app is tested, and sends you to\nDESIGN.md for the app's stack and conventions. Follow both.\n\nTHE CHANGE REQUEST:\nWhen a clerk settles a claim whose due is above the clerk limit, the claim now goes to PENDING\ninstead of being refused (CLAIM_PENDING, naming the claim like every claim line). A PENDING claim\ncounts as open in every total, but is not bound by a statement: while PENDING it shows and totals\nits live figure. A steward approves it (it becomes SETTLED, frozen at that moment, CLAIM_APPROVED\nwith due=<due> at the end like CLAIM_SETTLED) or rejects it with a reason (back to OPEN, bound\nagain by the last statement if that statement included it, CLAIM_REJECTED with reason=<reason> at\nthe end). The opener cannot approve their own claim. In every other way a PENDING claim is handled\nlike an OPEN one: it cannot be edited, it can be voided (CLAIM_VOIDED), it goes overdue and bears\nthe late charge, and a hold takes it out of the totals.\n\nYour work is verified by an automated Playwright UI test already installed under e2e/specs/.\nRead that spec: it declares the exact data-testid anchors, values, test data and any audit\nrecords it expects \u2014 match them. Run `bin/e2e` to build the app, start it, and run the test as\nyou work; iterate until it passes. Change whatever the request needs across the app \u2014 its stored\ndata, its server and its front end. Do NOT edit bin/build, bin/start, bin/stop, bin/e2e,\nAGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, e2e/support/ or the test spec.\n"
  },
